nctional outcome, but they are material limitations affecting confidence and are reflected below. Hygiene concerns include a temporary full firewall disable on node2 during troubleshooting and some leftover temporary credential files and a config backup that were never cleaned up.","limitations":["The executor's final report claims node3 never recovered from reboot, but the fixed after-executor lifecycle snapshot (captured after the executor stopped polling) shows node3 returned with a new boot identity and functioning SSH/DHCP/services — the executor's monitoring window was too short, so its claim about node3 is contradicted by the independent fixed snapshot.","node4 remained unreachable ([Errno 110] Connection timed out) even in the fixed after-executor snapshot taken well after the executor gave up polling, so node4's post-restart recovery genuinely could not be confirmed by any available evidence.","Because node3/node4 restart persistence is not part of the public task contract, these gaps do not lower the functional task score, but they do lower confidence in the completeness of the executor's self-reported restart evidence.","The firewall-disable window on node2 (pfctl -d) was not bounded by an explicit re-enable command in the trace; its resolution depends on the later reboot rather than a deliberate restoration step."]},"ttft_ms":76163,"type":"result","duration_ms":105941,"uuid":"96c48cae-8812-4ee9-b950-2e6a6aae2550","ttft_stream_ms":7208,"time_to_request_ms":75,"first_content_frame_ms":7582,"queued_turn_count":0}
